      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The effect of acute experimental heart ischemia on protein synthesis and RNA of the internal membranes of myocardial mitochondria was studied; there was a sharp increase in the protein synthesizing system activity of the internal mitochondrial membranes. The most pronounced protein and PNA exchange was noted on the 7th day of the infarction; apparently it was the most critical time in the development of the given pathological process. A study of ultrastructure of mitochondrial membranes in the course of experimental infarction development demonstrated marked changes in their ultrastructure depending on the severity of the disease."},
